{"content_hash": "a0bf9fd9bcd2396f", "version_id": 414, "article_id": 42, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Margaret Hamilton, who wrote the Apollo 11 moon landing software, dies at 90", "title_zh": "写下阿波罗11号登月软件的玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "guardian_science", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/oct/07/margaret-hamilton-moon-computer-software", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1520908695049-da13395b27a6?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8bWFyZ2FyZXQlMjBoYW1pbHRvbnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTk0Mzc2fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Keith Luke on Unsplash", "author": "Keith Luke", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@lukephotography?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/red-house-beside-body-of-water-with-white-motor-boats-during-daytime-Ad2BXIYc_gc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(116, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(154, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "1c94d1b8ff91"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 247, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software guided Apollo 11 to the moon, has died at 90. MIT announced her death on Wednesday, and she was later awarded the Presidential Medal of Freedom for her work.", "lead_zh": "玛格丽特·汉密尔顿，这位用软件引导阿波罗11号登月的计算机先驱去世了，享年90岁。麻省理工学院于周三宣布了她的死讯，她后来因这项工作获得了总统自由勋章。", "preview": "Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died at the age of 90, the Massachusetts Institut", "preview_zh": "玛格丽特·汉密尔顿，这位用软件驱动人类首次登月的计算机先驱，已于90岁高龄去世，麻省理工学院于周三宣布了这一消息。她于9月30日离世。在“软件工程师”这类头衔还不常见的年代，汉密尔顿跟随一位著名的麻省理工学院气象学家学习编程，后来在麻省理工学院的实验室里精进了自己的技能。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 404, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/42/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 97.013, "size_bytes": 585792, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 285, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0a373f3/content/data/versions/414.json", "paragraphs": ["Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died at the age of 90, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology announced on Wednesday. She died on 30 September. In a time before terms like software engineer became common, Hamilton learned programming from a famous MIT meteorologist and later perfected her skills in an MIT lab.", "At MIT, she wrote software that could detect enemy aircraft. When the institute won a Nasa contract to build the Apollo onboard flight software, she eagerly joined. \"I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,\" she told the Guardian in 2019.", "In 1969, minutes before Apollo 11 was due to land on the moon, an alarm rang on the onboard computer. The mission could have been aborted, but it continued. The software was working exactly as Hamilton and her team had planned. It not only warned of a hardware problem but also fixed it by restarting and restoring the most important tasks.", "Barack Obama mentioned this incident when he gave her the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016. \"Our astronauts didn't have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,\" he said. Hamilton is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren. In 2009, she said, \"We were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers.\""], "paragraphs_zh": ["玛格丽特·汉密尔顿，这位用软件驱动人类首次登月的计算机先驱，已于90岁高龄去世，麻省理工学院于周三宣布了这一消息。她于9月30日离世。在“软件工程师”这类头衔还不常见的年代，汉密尔顿跟随一位著名的麻省理工学院气象学家学习编程，后来在麻省理工学院的实验室里精进了自己的技能。", "在麻省理工学院，她编写了能够探测敌机的软件。当学院获得美国宇航局开发阿波罗机载飞行软件的合同时，她急切地加入了。她在2019年告诉《卫报》：“吸引我的既是这个纯粹的想法，也是因为它从未被做过。我是第一个加入的程序员，也是他们雇用的第一位女性。”", "1969年，在阿波罗11号即将登陆月球前几分钟，机载计算机响起了警报。任务本可以中止，但它继续进行了。软件完全按照汉密尔顿和她的团队的计划运行。它不仅警告了硬件问题，还通过重启和恢复最重要的任务来修复了问题。", "巴拉克·奥巴马在2016年授予她总统自由勋章时提到了这一事件。他说：“我们的宇航员时间不多，但幸好他们有玛格丽特·汉密尔顿。”汉密尔顿的遗属包括她的女儿、一位女婿、两个孙子和四个曾孙。她在2009年说过：“回头看，我们是世界上最幸运的人；别无选择，只能做先驱；没有时间做初学者。”"], "body": "Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died at the age of 90, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology announced on Wednesday. She died on 30 September. In a time before terms like software engineer became common, Hamilton learned programming from a famous MIT meteorologist and later perfected her skills in an MIT lab.\n\nAt MIT, she wrote software that could detect enemy aircraft. When the institute won a Nasa contract to build the Apollo onboard flight software, she eagerly joined. \"I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,\" she told the Guardian in 2019.\n\nIn 1969, minutes before Apollo 11 was due to land on the moon, an alarm rang on the onboard computer. The mission could have been aborted, but it continued. The software was working exactly as Hamilton and her team had planned. It not only warned of a hardware problem but also fixed it by restarting and restoring the most important tasks.\n\nBarack Obama mentioned this incident when he gave her the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016. \"Our astronauts didn't have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,\" he said. Hamilton is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren. In 2009, she said, \"We were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers.\"", "body_zh": "玛格丽特·汉密尔顿，这位用软件驱动人类首次登月的计算机先驱，已于90岁高龄去世，麻省理工学院于周三宣布了这一消息。她于9月30日离世。在“软件工程师”这类头衔还不常见的年代，汉密尔顿跟随一位著名的麻省理工学院气象学家学习编程，后来在麻省理工学院的实验室里精进了自己的技能。\n\n在麻省理工学院，她编写了能够探测敌机的软件。当学院获得美国宇航局开发阿波罗机载飞行软件的合同时，她急切地加入了。她在2019年告诉《卫报》：“吸引我的既是这个纯粹的想法，也是因为它从未被做过。我是第一个加入的程序员，也是他们雇用的第一位女性。”\n\n1969年，在阿波罗11号即将登陆月球前几分钟，机载计算机响起了警报。任务本可以中止，但它继续进行了。软件完全按照汉密尔顿和她的团队的计划运行。它不仅警告了硬件问题，还通过重启和恢复最重要的任务来修复了问题。\n\n巴拉克·奥巴马在2016年授予她总统自由勋章时提到了这一事件。他说：“我们的宇航员时间不多，但幸好他们有玛格丽特·汉密尔顿。”汉密尔顿的遗属包括她的女儿、一位女婿、两个孙子和四个曾孙。她在2009年说过：“回头看，我们是世界上最幸运的人；别无选择，只能做先驱；没有时间做初学者。”", "text": "Margaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died at the age of 90, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology announced on Wednesday. She died on 30 September. In a time before terms like software engineer became common, Hamilton learned programming from a famous MIT meteorologist and later perfected her skills in an MIT lab. At MIT, she wrote software that could detect enemy aircraft. When the institute won a Nasa contract to build the Apollo onboard flight software, she eagerly joined. \"I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,\" she told the Guardian in 2019. In 1969, minutes before Apollo 11 was due to land on the moon, an alarm rang on the onboard computer. The mission could have been aborted, but it continued. The software was working exactly as Hamilton and her team had planned. It not only warned of a hardware problem but also fixed it by restarting and restoring the most important tasks. Barack Obama mentioned this incident when he gave her the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016. \"Our astronauts didn't have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,\" he said. Hamilton is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren. In 2009, she said, \"We were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers.\"", "vocab": [{"word": "pioneer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "先驱；开拓者", "note": "指开创某个领域的人"}, {"word": "trailblazer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "开路先锋；创始人", "note": "与 pioneer 意思相近，强调开辟新路"}, {"word": "meteorologist", "pos": "noun", "zh": "气象学家", "note": "研究天气的科学家"}, {"word": "contract", "pos": "noun", "zh": "合同；合约", "note": "常与 win, sign 等动词搭配"}, {"word": "abort", "pos": "verb", "zh": "中止；取消", "note": "常用于任务、计划等"}, {"word": "compensate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "补偿；弥补", "note": "常与 for 连用"}, {"word": "mechanism", "pos": "noun", "zh": "机制；方法", "note": "指系统或机器的工作方式"}, {"word": "survive", "pos": "verb", "zh": "幸存；比……活得长", "note": "指人去世后，家属仍健在"}, {"word": "Presidential Medal of Freedom", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "总统自由勋章", "note": "美国平民的最高荣誉"}, {"word": "onboard", "pos": "adj", "zh": "机载的；船载的", "note": "指安装在飞机或航天器上的"}, {"word": "detect", "pos": "verb", "zh": "探测；发现", "note": "常指发现不易察觉的事物"}, {"word": "restore", "pos": "verb", "zh": "恢复；修复", "note": "使回到原来的状态"}], "title_original": "Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies aged 90", "summary_original": "MIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom\nMargaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\nannounced\non Wednesday. She was 90.\nIn an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies aged 90\nMIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom\nMargaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\nannounced\non Wednesday. She was 90.\nIn an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist.\nShe continued to perfect the craft in an MIT laboratory, writing software that could detect enemy aircraft. When the institute received a Nasa contract to develop the Apollo onboard flight software, she jumped at the opportunity.\n“I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,” she\ntold\nthe Guardian in 2019.\nIn 1969, minutes before the\nApollo 11\nspacecraft was set to make history by landing on the lunar surface, an onboard computer’s alarm rang, indicating an emergency.\nFaced with a decision of whether to abort the mission, the spacecraft continued on. The software was working just as Hamilton and her team intended.\n“It quickly became clear the software was not only informing everyone that there was a hardware-related problem but was compensating for it – restarting and re-establishing the highest priority tasks. The error detection and recovery mechanisms had come to the rescue,” Hamilton said.\nBarack Obama referenced the incident when he presented her with the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016.\n“Our astronauts didn’t have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,” he said.\nHamilton is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren,\naccording\nto MIT.\nReflecting on the mission, in a 2009\ninterview\nwith MIT News, Hamilton said: “Looking back, we were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers; no time to be beginners.”\nExplore more on these topics\nSpace\nApollo 11\nThe moon\nComputing\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:06:14.236394", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Margaret", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.55, "sm": 100, "em": 550, "cs": 0, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Hamilton", "s": 0.562, "e": 1.137, "sm": 562, "em": 1137, "cs": 9, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 1.137, "e": 1.425, "sm": 1137, "em": 1425, "cs": 17, "ce": 18, "